{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q420172","formula":"C₁₄H₁₈N₄O₃","hill":"C14H18N4O3","elements":["H","C","N","O"],"composition":{"C":14.0,"H":18.0,"N":4.0,"O":3.0},"names":{"en":"Benomyl","ru":"Беномил"},"descriptions":{"en":"Benomyl (also marketed as Benlate) is a fungicide introduced in 1968 by DuPont. It is a systemic benzimidazole fungicide that is selectively toxic to microorganisms and invertebrates (especially earthworms), but relatively nontoxic toward mammals. Due to the prevalence of resistance of parasitic fungi to benomyl, it and similar pesticides are of diminished effectiveness.","ru":"Беномил (1-(бутилкарбамоил)-1H-1,3-бензимидазол-2-ил метилкарбамат, бенлат, узген, фундазол) — непредельное органическое соединение. Системный фунгицид, эффективный для борьбы с рядом заболеваний растений. Получают взаимодействием карбендазима с бутилизоцианатом."},"fame":16,"pubchemCid":28780,"mass":290.32,"charge":0,"smiles":"CCCCNC(=O)N1C2=CC=CC=C2N=C1NC(=O)OC","inchikey":"RIOXQFHNBCKOKP-UHFFFAOYSA-N","iupac":"methyl N-[1-(butylcarbamoyl)benzimidazol-2-yl]carbamate","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"28780","atoms":39,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":0.141,"y":2.147,"z":0.222,"el":"O"},{"x":-4.041,"y":2.219,"z":0.179,"el":"O"},{"x":-4.343,"y":-0.046,"z":0.156,"el":"O"},{"x":-0.002,"y":-0.087,"z":-0.126,"el":"N"},{"x":1.879,"y":1.039,"z":-0.883,"el":"N"},{"x":-1.822,"y":-1.408,"z":-0.037,"el":"N"},{"x":-2.206,"y":0.922,"z":0.033,"el":"N"},{"x":3.695,"y":2.478,"z":-0.031,"el":"C"},{"x":2.701,"y":2.197,"z":-1.152,"el":"C"},{"x":0.461,"y":-1.401,"z":-0.061,"el":"C"},{"x":4.678,"y":1.325,"z":0.186,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.696,"y":-2.185,"z":-0.042,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.38,"y":-0.175,"z":-0.043,"el":"C"},{"x":0.678,"y":1.139,"z":-0.219,"el":"C"},{"x":1.733,"y":-1.989,"z":0.03